## Context

Some projects hand-maintain quantitative sections in STATE.md (e.g.
climate-finance-het `## Corpus` / `## Health`) that a project command could
regenerate; hand-refreshing them is where their staleness risk lives. The
harness script must stay project-agnostic, so the metrics command belongs to
the project: an extension point, not harness-baked logic.

## Relevant files
- `scripts/refresh-STATE.py` — insertion into the generated block
- `rules/state.md` — document the contract

## Actions
1. Define the contract: if the repo declares a metrics command (proposed: a
   `state-metrics` make target; alternatives welcome), `refresh-STATE.py` runs
   it and appends its stdout lines to the generated `## Status` block.
2. Failure or absence of the target degrades to the plain block — never blocks
   the refresh.
3. Document the contract in `rules/state.md`; count metrics lines against the
   ≤ 20-line Status budget.

## Test
- Fixture repo with a `state-metrics` target → lines appear in the block.
- No target / failing target → plain block, exit 0.

## Verification
- [ ] Harness repo (no target) refreshes unchanged
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Invariants
- No project-specific logic in the harness script.

## Exit criteria
- A project can regenerate its metrics lines through the standard refresh,
  opt-in, with graceful degradation; documented and tested.
